+## Mini Server Access
+
+The Mini should keep `com.saneapps.always-awake` loaded, `work_session_on`
+state active, SSH reachable as `mini`, and Codex remote control connected.
+`scripts/mini/mini-codex-keepalive.sh` is the durable five-minute LaunchAgent
+path for Codex access: it bootstraps/enables the managed app-server daemon,
+starts remote control, and runs bounded desktop hygiene without quitting Codex.
+The unattended path defaults `SANE_MINI_ALLOW_SYSTEM_EVENTS=0`; do not use
+shell-driven `System Events` cleanup on the travel server unless a human is
+present to accept macOS Automation prompts. Safari is preserved for App Store
+Connect and Lemon Squeezy sessions: cleanup minimizes Safari instead of quitting
+it, and keepalive touches already-open portal tabs on a bounded interval
+without opening new login surfaces.
+
+Quick checks:
+
+```bash
+ssh mini 'hostname; whoami'
+/Applications/Codex.app/Contents/Resources/codex remote-control start --json
+launchctl print gui/$(id -u)/com.saneapps.codex-keepalive
+ruby scripts/SaneMaster.rb work_session_status
